2. CRSB (phones and meters): +0.085 dB when dimmed (the C/ROOM pot no longer loads the 100R build-out)

3. switching step: per 1 mV of DC on CRSB (the CRS follower's offset; its input sits on 100K // 1M to GNDA)
   C/ROOM 1.0: step 0.88 mV at the C/Room follower =  -58.9 dBu peak,  -52.9 dBu at the TRS output (DRV135 +6 dB); decays with tau 0.22 s
               with TI's model (0.50 mV): 0.44 mV,  -64.9 dBu at the follower,  -58.9 dBu at the TRS output
   C/ROOM 0.7: step 0.42 mV at the C/Room follower =  -65.3 dBu peak,  -59.3 dBu at the TRS output (DRV135 +6 dB); decays with tau 0.22 s
               with TI's model (0.50 mV): 0.21 mV,  -71.4 dBu at the follower,  -65.4 dBu at the TRS output
   C/ROOM 0.5: step 0.13 mV at the C/Room follower =  -75.5 dBu peak,  -69.5 dBu at the TRS output (DRV135 +6 dB); decays with tau 0.22 s
               with TI's model (0.50 mV): 0.06 mV,  -81.6 dBu at the follower,  -75.6 dBu at the TRS output
   a step whose spectrum falls 6 dB / octave: mostly LF. For the PFL switcher's ticks see master spec section 19

